digraph account_payable_process_153 {
	graph [rankdir=LR]
	START_NODE [label="" shape=circle width=0.3]
	subgraph CLUSTER_0 {
		"send to the vendor accounting department" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" [shape=box]
		"send to the vendor accounting department" -> "create a receiving report"
		"report errors to relevant team member" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" -> "report errors to relevant team member"
		"schedule the payment" [shape=box]
		"report errors to relevant team member" -> "schedule the payment"
	}
	START_NODE -> "send to the vendor accounting department"
	END_NODE [label="" shape=doublecircle width=0.2]
	"schedule the payment" -> END_NODE
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The following description is about the account payable process. It starts with sending to the vendor accounting department. 
When sending to the vendor accounting department is completed, creating a receiving report needs to be done. 
Once creating a receiving report occurs, reporting errors to relevant team member should be done. 
When reporting errors to relevant team member is completed, scheduling the payment should be done. 
The process is now completed. 
"
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The following description is about the account payable process, which begins with sending to the vendor accounting department.
When the sending to vendor accounting department is completed, a receiving report needs to be created.
Once a receiving report is created, reporting errors should be done to the relevant team member.
When the reporting error is completed to the relevant team member, the payments should be booked.
The process is completed now.
